# avalio-backend

FastAPI backend for **Avaliario** — a teacher-focused student evaluation system with admin-controlled accounts, full audit logging, and JWT authentication.

## Stack

| Layer | Tech |
|---|---|
| Framework | FastAPI + Uvicorn |
| ORM | SQLAlchemy 2.0 (Mapped[] style) |
| Migrations | Alembic |
| Database | SQLite (local) → PostgreSQL (VPS) |
| Auth | JWT access tokens + DB-persisted refresh tokens |
| Password hashing | passlib + bcrypt <4 |
| Validation | Pydantic v2 + email-validator |
| Package manager | uv |

## Project structure

```
avalio-backend/
├── alembic/
│   ├── env.py              # Migration environment, imports all models
│   └── script.py.mako      # Migration file template
├── app/
│   ├── config.py           # Settings via pydantic-settings (.env)
│   ├── database.py         # SQLAlchemy engine, SessionLocal, Base
│   ├── main.py             # FastAPI app, router registration, /health
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── user.py         # User, UserRole enum
│   │   ├── refresh_token.py
│   │   ├── student.py      # Student (soft-delete via archived_at)
│   │   ├── class_.py       # Class, ClassStudent (enrollment join table)
│   │   ├── evaluation.py   # Evaluation, EvaluationEntry, EvaluationEntryHistory
│   │   └── audit_log.py    # Immutable audit records
│   ├── schemas/            # Pydantic request/response models
│   ├── routers/
│   │   ├── auth.py         # POST /auth/login, /refresh, /logout
│   │   ├── admin.py        # GET/POST /admin/users, PATCH approve/deactivate
│   │   ├── students.py     # CRUD + archive, teacher-scoped
│   │   ├── classes.py      # CRUD + student enrollment
│   │   ├── evaluations.py  # CRUD + grade entry upsert with history
│   │   └── audit.py        # GET /audit/ (admin only)
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── security.py     # hash_password, verify_password, JWT creation/decode
│   │   ├── dependencies.py # get_db, get_current_user, require_admin
│   │   └── exceptions.py   # AvalioError + handler
│   └── services/
│       └── audit.py        # audit.log() — writes AuditLog, flushes (not commits)
├── seed.py                 # Creates initial admin account
├── alembic.ini
├── pyproject.toml
└── .env.example
```

## Setup

```bash
cp .env.example .env
# edit .env — set SECRET_KEY at minimum

uv sync
uv run alembic upgrade head
uv run python seed.py        # creates admin user rut / testing
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000 --host 0.0.0.0 --reload
```

API docs available at `http://localhost:8000/docs`.

## Environment variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | `sqlite:///./avalio.db` | SQLAlchemy connection string |
| `SECRET_KEY` | — | JWT signing key (required) |
| `ALGORITHM` | `HS256` | JWT algorithm |
| `ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES` | `15` | Access token lifetime |
| `REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS` | `30` | Refresh token lifetime |

## Auth design

- Access tokens are short-lived JWTs (15 min), held in memory by the client.
- Refresh tokens are stored in the database, enabling revocation on logout or account deactivation.
- Refresh token rotation: each `/auth/refresh` call revokes the old token and issues a new pair.
- Login uses a `_DUMMY_HASH` constant-time check even when the username doesn't exist, preventing user enumeration via timing.

## Roles

| Role | Permissions |
|---|---|
| `admin` | Full access to all resources, user management, audit log |
| `teacher` | Access only to their own classes and enrolled students |

Teachers cannot see students or classes that aren't theirs. Access is enforced at the query level (not just in response filtering).

## Audit logging

Every state-changing operation writes an `AuditLog` record via `audit.log()` before committing. The log entry and the action share the same database transaction — either both persist or neither does.

Fields logged: `actor_id`, `action`, `target_type`, `target_id`, `detail` (JSON), `timestamp`, `ip_address`.

## Grade history

Every time an `EvaluationEntry` is updated, the previous `grade` and `note` values are snapshotted into `EvaluationEntryHistory` before overwriting. This table is append-only and never modified after insert.

---

## What's done

- [x] All models with relationships
- [x] Alembic migration environment
- [x] JWT auth with refresh token rotation and revocation
- [x] `TokenResponse` includes `role` so the client can gate UI without decoding the JWT
- [x] Admin: create/approve/deactivate/reset-password users
- [x] Change password (`POST /auth/change-password`) — revokes all refresh tokens on success
- [x] Students: create, read, update, archive (soft-delete); paginated
- [x] Classes: create, list, add/remove students, `GET /{class_id}/students`; all paginated
- [x] Evaluations: create, list, grade entry upsert with history, `GET /{evaluation_id}/entries`; all paginated
- [x] Audit log: all write operations logged, queryable by admins; paginated
- [x] Teacher scoping on students, classes, and evaluations
- [x] Seed script for first admin account

## What's left to do

- [ ] **PostgreSQL support** — switch `DATABASE_URL` and test; SQLite-specific `check_same_thread` flag needs to be conditional
- [ ] **CORS configuration** — currently no CORS middleware; needed if a web frontend is ever added
- [ ] **Rate limiting** — login endpoint has no brute-force protection beyond the timing-safe dummy hash
- [ ] **Tests** — no test suite exists yet; at minimum auth, access control, and audit log coverage
- [ ] **Deployment config** — no Dockerfile, systemd unit, or reverse proxy config for VPS deployment
